An electronic system (10) for managing digital content relating to works of art is described, the system comprising:

- a first electronic processing unit (11), configured to acquire, generate, store, process and/or transmit digital content associated with at least one work of art, said digital content comprising one or more of: image data, video data, audio data, descriptive data, authentication data, provenance data, ownership data, restoration data, exhibition data, metadata, certificates, and transaction records;
- encryption/decryption means (11a) operatively associated with said first electronic processing unit (11), configured to encrypt at least part of said digital content before storage and/or transmission and to decrypt said digital content upon authorization;
- a second electronic processing unit (12), configured to receive, access, verify, display and/or further process said digital content relating to the work of art;
- communication means configured to allow data exchange between said first electronic processing unit (11) and said second electronic processing unit (12), preferably through a wired or wireless communication network.

In one embodiment, the first electronic processing unit (11) is associated with a provider, owner, curator, museum, gallery, artist, authentication body, archive or management platform for works of art. The second electronic processing unit (12) may be associated with a user, purchaser, viewer, verifier, museum operator, gallery operator, insurer, registrar, restorer or certifying entity.

The encryption/decryption means (11a) may comprise hardware and/or software modules adapted to perform symmetric encryption, asymmetric encryption, hashing, digital signature generation, digital signature verification, key management and/or secure authentication. The encryption/decryption means (11a) may further be configured to associate the digital content with a unique identifier of the corresponding work of art, thereby enabling secure traceability of said digital content.

A method (100) for managing digital content relating to works of art by means of the electronic system (10) comprises the following steps:

- step (110): acquiring and/or generating digital content relating to at least one work of art, said digital content including one or more data items representative of the work of art, its author, provenance, authenticity, ownership, conservation state, exhibition history and/or associated rights;
- step (150): encrypting, by means of the encryption/decryption means (11a) of the first electronic processing unit (11), at least part of the digital content relating to the work of art, thereby generating encrypted digital content;
- step (160): transmitting and/or making available the encrypted digital content from the first electronic processing unit (11) to the second electronic processing unit (12), through said communication means;
- step (170): decrypting, by means of the encryption/decryption means (11a) and/or corresponding decryption means available to the second electronic processing unit (12), the encrypted digital content following verification of an authorization condition;
- step (180): displaying, storing, validating, certifying, updating and/or otherwise processing the decrypted digital content at the second electronic processing unit (12), thereby enabling secure management of information relating to the corresponding work of art.

In a preferred embodiment, the authorization condition comprises at least one of: user authentication, password verification, biometric verification, possession of a cryptographic key, validation of an access token, verification of a digital certificate, confirmation of ownership rights, confirmation of viewing rights, or verification of a transaction record.

The method (100) may further comprise associating the digital content with a unique code, such as a QR code, RFID identifier, NFC tag, blockchain token, serial number or digital fingerprint corresponding to the work of art. Said unique code may be applied to, stored with, or otherwise linked to the work of art, its frame, support, certificate, archive entry or digital twin.

The system (10) and method (100) advantageously allow controlled access to digital content relating to works of art, while maintaining confidentiality, authenticity, integrity and traceability of said content. The invention is particularly suitable for use in digital art archives, museum databases, online galleries, art marketplaces, authenticity certification systems, provenance tracking systems, insurance systems and restoration documentation platforms.
